hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"11","Abd al-Rahman bin Bishr bin al-Hakam and my uncle Ismail bin Khuzaymah narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Hammam. Ibn Munabbih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The prayer of any of you will not be accepted if he breaks his fast, until he performs ablution.”"
"12","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan. H Abu Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, meaning Ibn Mahdi, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Sulayman bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform ablution at every prayer, so when the day of the conquest came, he ablution and wiped over He hid it, and performed the prayers with one ablution.” Then Omar said to him: “O Messenger of God, you have done something that you did not do.” He said: “I intentionally I did it, O Omar.” This is the hadith of Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi"
"13","Ali bin Al-Hussein Al-Durhami narrated to us a strange news. He said: Mu’tamar narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of his father, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform ablution for every prayer, except on the day of the conquest of Mecca, for he was busy, so he combined between noon and afternoon with one ablution.”"
"14","Abu Ammar told us, Waki` bin al-Jarrah told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Sulayman bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to perform ablution for every prayer, so when it was the day of the conquest of Mecca, he performed all the prayers with one ablution.” Abu Bakr said: This report was not narrated on the authority of Al-Thawri by anyone we know other than Al-Mu`tamir and Al-Waki’. It was narrated by the companions of Al-Thawri and others, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muharib, on the authority of Suleiman bin Buraidah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so if Al-Mu'tamir and Wakee' along with their majesty preserved this chain of narration and its continuity, so it is strange news."
"15","Muhammad ibn Mansour Abu Jaafar and Muhammad ibn Shukar ibn Rafi’ al-Baghdadi narrated to us, saying: Ya’qub narrated to us, and he is the son of Abraham. Bin Saad, my father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban Al-Ansari told us, then Al-Mazani Mazin Bani Al-Najjar, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar. H Muhammad bin Yahya narrated to us, Ahmad bin Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban. On the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Omar, he said: I said to him: Have you seen Abdullah bin Omar’s ablution for every prayer, whether he was pure or impure, for whom? Him? He said: It was narrated to him by Asma’ bint Zayd bin Al-Khattab, that Abdullah bin Hanzala bin Abi Amir Al-Ghassil narrated to her, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He commanded that ablution be performed at every prayer, whether one is pure or impure. When that was difficult for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He commanded the use of the siwak at every prayer, and ablution was removed from it except in the case of an event.” Abdullah believed that he had the strength to do that, so he did it until he died. This is the hadith of Yaqoub bin Ibrahim, except that Muhammad bin Mansour said: He used to do it until he died."
"16","Muhammad ibn Bashar Bundar told us, Muhammad i.e. Ibn Ja`far told us, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara, about the fight. Ibn Sabra, that he witnessed Ali praying the noon prayer, then he sat in the spacious area attending to the people’s needs. When the afternoon prayer came, he called for a basin of water and wiped it with it. His arms, face, head, and legs, then he drank the remainder of his ablution while standing, then he said: Some people hate to drink while they are standing. Standing up. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did the same as what I did, and he said: “This is the ablution of one who does not perform it.” Yusuf bin Musa told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour bin Al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Maysara, on the authority of Al-Nazzal bin Sabra, So he mentioned the hadith and said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do as I did, and he said: “This is the ablution of one who does not perform it.” Abu Bakr said: It was narrated by Mis’ar bin Kadam, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Maysarah, on the authority of Al-Nazzal bin Sabra, on the authority of Ali, and he said: Then He said: “This is the ablution of one who does not perform it.” Yusuf bin Musa narrated to us, Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, and Ubayd Allah bin Musa narrated to us."
"17","Ahmad bin Ubaidah al-Dhabi told us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zaid, told us on the authority of Asim. H Ali bin Khashram told us, Ibn Uyaynah told us, Asim told us. H Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makhzoumi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Al-Najjoud, on the authority of Zirr bin Hubaysh, he said: I came Safwan bin Assal Al-Muradi I asked him about wiping over the socks, and he said: What brings you, Zurr? I said: Seeking knowledge. He said: “O button! For the angels spread their wings for the seeker of knowledge, satisfied with what he seeks.” He said: So I said: Something occurred to me about wiping over the socks after defecating, and I was one of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. Did you hear the Messenger of God mention anything of that? He said: “Yes, he used to order us, when we were traveling, or he said traveling, not to remove our socks for three days and their nights, except out of ritual impurity, but only from Stool, urinate, and sleep.” This is the hadith of Al-Makhzoumi, and Ahmad bin Abdah said in his hadith: He said: I have been informed that the angels lower their wings"
"18","Ahmad ibn Mani’, Ya’qub ibn Ibrahim al-Durqi, Muhammad ibn Hisham, and Fadalah ibn al-Fadl al-Kufi narrated to us. They said: narrated to us. Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, Ahmad bin Mani’ said: He said: Abu Husayn told us, and the others said: On the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Sulami, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, said: I was a man who was ill-advised, so I was ashamed to ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, because his daughter I had it, so I ordered a man to ask him and he said: “Ablution is part of it.”"
"19","Bishr bin Khaled Al-Askari told us, Muhammad bin Jafar told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Suleiman, who is Al-Amash, speaking, on the authority of Mundhir Al-Thawri, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali, on the authority of Ali, said: I was ashamed to ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about pre-ejaculatory fluid for the sake of Fatima, so I ordered Al-Miqdad ibn Al-Aswad, and he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that, and he said: “Ablution is required of it.”"
"20","Ali bin Hajar Al-Saadi and Bishr bin Muadh Al-Aqdi told us, saying: Ubaida bin Humaid told us, Ali said: He said: Tell me. H And Bishr said: He said: Al-Rukain bin Al-Rabi’ bin Umaylah told us, on the authority of Husayn bin Qubaisa, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, he said: I was a man Then I started bathing in the winter until my back cracked, so I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, or it was mentioned to him, and he said to me: “Don’t do it. “If you see precum, wash your penis, and perform your ablution for prayer, and if you sprinkle water, then perform ablution.” Abu Bakr said: His saying: “Do not do it” is of the kind that I would say is a reprehensible word, meaning to deny the obligation of that action."
"21","Yunus bin Abd al-Ala al-Sadfi told us, Ibn Wahb told us, that Malik bin Anas told him, on the authority of Abu al-Nadr, the client of Omar bin Ubaid. By God, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yassar, on the authority of Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad, that Ali bin Abi Talib ordered him to ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Concerning a man, if he approaches his family and pre-eclampsia comes out of him, what does he have to do? Ali said: I have the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I am ashamed to ask him. Al-Miqdad said: So I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace about that, and he said: “If one of you finds that, let him clean his private parts, and let him perform his ablution for prayer.”"
"22","Ahmad bin Abdul Rahman bin Wahb bin Muslim told us, my uncle told us, Makhramah, meaning Ibn Bukayr, told me on the authority of his father, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: Ali bin Abi Talib said: I sent Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad to the Messenger of God, may God bless him. He greeted him and asked him about pre-ejaculatory fluid coming out of a person. What should he do? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Perform ablution and clean your private parts.”"
"23","Muhammad bin Saeed bin Ghalib Abu Yahya Al-Attar narrated to us, Ubaidah bin Humayd narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, who said: I was a man in distress, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about me. He acknowledged that and said: “Ablution is sufficient for you.” Abu Bakr said: In the report of Sahl ibn Hunaif, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who was in pre-ejaculatory fluid, he said: “That ablution is sufficient for you.” I mentioned it in the chapter on sprinkling precum from the garment."
"24","Ahmad bin Abdah al-Dhabi told us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad al-Darawardi. H Abu Bishr al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khaled narrated to us, meaning Ibn Abdullah, both of them, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you finds something in his stomach, and it is doubtful whether something came out of it or not, then they should not take it out.” Until he hears a sound, or smells a wind.” This is the hadith of Khalid bin Abdullah"
"25","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us, Al-Zuhri told us, Abbad bin Tamim told me, on the authority of his uncle Abdullah bin Zayd. He said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about a man who finds something while he is praying, and he said: “He does not leave until he hears a sound or finds \"wind\""
"26","Ali bin Khashram told us, Isa, meaning Ibn Yunus, told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan, who is Ibn Atiyya, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Abi Aisha, he said: Abu Hurairah told me that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The servant will continue to pray as long as the prayer detains him, unless “It happens.” Al-Ahdāt means: to make a mistake or to make a mistake. I am not ashamed of what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not ashamed of."
"27","Muhammad bin Bashar narrated to us, Muhammad bin Jaafar narrated to us, Shu’bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Suhail bin Abi Saleh narrating, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. H. Salam bin Junada told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah. H, Bundar told us, and Abu Musa told us, saying: Abd al-Rahman told us, Shu’bah told us. H Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala narrated to us, Khalid, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, narrated to us, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no ablution except from sound or wind.”"
"28","Abu Bishr al-Wasiti told us, Khalid, meaning Ibn Abdullah al-Wasiti, told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you finds something in his stomach and is unsure whether something came out of it or not, then let them not come out until He hears a sound or feels a wind.”"
"29","Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muadh bin Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, Iyad narrated to me, He asked Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. H, Salam bin Junada al-Qurashi told us, Waki` told us, Ali bin al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Iyad bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The devil comes to one of you during your prayer and says: You “You have told something, so let him say: You lied, unless he smells it in his nose or hears its voice with his ear.” This is an adequate word. Abu Bakr said: His saying: Let him say, “You lied.” He meant: Let him say, “You lied” with his conscience. He does not speak with his tongue, since it is not permissible for the praying person to say: He says you lied out loud"
"30","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman Al-Muradi narrated to us, Shu’ayb, meaning Ibn Al-Layth, narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ja’far bin Rabi’ah, who is Ibn Shuhrabil. Ibn Hasanah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz, said: Abu Hurairah said, preferring him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Every son Adam was inevitably afflicted with fornication, for the eye’s fornication is looking, the hand’s fornication is touching, the soul desires or talks, and he believes him or her. Distraction belieth him.” Abu Bakr said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught that touching may be with the hand. God Almighty said: Even if We had sent down to you a book in Paper, so they touched it with their hands. Surat Al-An'am, verse 7. Our Lord, the Almighty and Majestic, knew that touching might be with the hand, and so did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he forbade Regarding the touch sale, the prohibition on touch selling indicated to them that touching is done with the hand, which is for the buyer to touch the garment without turning it over and spreading it, He says when making a purchase: If I touch the garment with my hand, I have no choice anymore if I look at the length and width of the garment or if any defect appears on it. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ma’iz ibn Malik when he confessed to him about adultery: Perhaps you kissed or touched, so this word indicates He only meant when he said: Or touched something other than intercourse that would entail punishment, and likewise the story of Aisha. Abu Bakr said: He did not disagree. Our scholars from the Hijazis, the Egyptians, the Shafi’is, and the Ahl al-Athar state that the qiblah and touching with the hand, if it is not between the hand and the body If a woman is touched by a veil, a cover of clothing, or anything else, that requires ablution, except that Malik ibn Anas used to say: If The kiss and the touching with the hand was not a kiss of desire, as that does not require ablution. Abu Bakr said: This word: And he is believed or disbelieved by the private parts: from the type that I was taught in the Book of Faith that belief may occur with some of the limbs, not as those who claimed Some people misrepresented that belief in the Arabic language only comes from the heart. I have explained this issue completely in the Book of Faith."
"31","Bishr bin Muadh Al-Aqdi told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Abdullah bin Mawhib, on the authority of Ja’far bin Abi Thawr, On the authority of Jabir bin Samra, that a man asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, should I perform ablution with sheep meat? He said: “If you wish, perform ablution, and if you wish, do not perform ablution.” He said: Should I perform ablution with camel meat? He said: “Yes, I will perform ablution with camel meat.” He said: Should I pray in sheep stalls? He said: “Yes.” He said: Should I pray in a camel shed? He said: “No.” Abu Bakr said: We did not see any disagreement among the scholars of Ahl al-Hadith that this news is authentic in terms of transmission. He also narrated this news: on the authority of Ja'far bin Abi Thawr, Ash'ath bin Abi Al-Sha'ath'a Al-Muharribi, and Sammak bin Harb, these are three of the most prominent narrators of the hadith. On the authority of Jafar bin Abi Thawr this news"
"32","Muhammad bin Yahya also narrated to us, Muhadhar Al-Hamdani narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah, who is Al-Razi, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of al-Baraa ibn Azib, he said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “I will pray in... Blessed are the camels? He said: “No.” He said: “Should I perform ablution from their meat?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Should I perform ablution from sheep pens?” He said: “Yes.” Its meat? He said: “No.” Abu Bakr said: We did not see any disagreement among the scholars of the hadith scholars that this news is also true from the point of view of fairness of transmission. Its carriers"
"33","Muhammad bin Al-Alaa bin Kurayb Al-Hamdani told us, and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak Al-Mukhurami told us, saying: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Marwan, on the authority of Busra bint Safwan, that she heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “If he touches “If one of you mentions it, let him perform ablution.” I heard Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sadfi, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Malik, who said: I view ablution after touching the penis as desirable, but not I answer him. Ali bin Saeed Al-Nasawi narrated to us, saying: I asked Ahmad bin Hanbal about performing ablution after touching the penis, and he said: I recommend it but do not make it obligatory."
"34","And I heard Muhammad bin Yahya saying: We view ablution after touching the penis as a recommendation, not an obligation, according to the hadith of Abdullah bin Badr, on the authority of Qais bin He divorced, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Abu Bakr said: Al-Shafi’i, may God have mercy on him, made it obligatory to perform ablution after touching the penis, following the report of Busra bint Safwan, not by analogy. Abu Bakr: And according to Al-Shafi’i, I say, because Urwa heard good news from her, not as some of our scholars imagined that the news is weak. For stabbing Marwan"
"35","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim, Ziyad bin Ayyub, and Ma’mal bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Ismail, who is Ibn Ulayya, narrated to us. He said: Ziyad: He said: Ayoub told us, and the other two said: On the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He came out of the open space, and food was brought to him, and they said: Shall we not bring you ablution? He said: “I was only ordered to perform ablution when I stand up to pray.” Al-Dawraqi said: for prayer"
"36","Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb Al-Hamdani told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Sadaqa bin Yasar told us, On the authority of Ibn Jabir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah. H Muhammad bin Issa narrated to us, Salamah, meaning Ibn al-Fadl, narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, Sadaqa bin Yasar narrated to me, on the authority of Aqeel bin Jabir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: “We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the battle against Dhat al-Riqa’ of palm trees, and he was struck A man from among the Muslims, the wife of a man from among the polytheists. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, departed in a caravan, her husband came and was absent. The news was told that he swore and would not stop until he shed blood among the companions of Muhammad, so he went out following in the footsteps of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God descended. A house, and he said: Who is there to take care of us this night? So a man from the Muhajireen and a man from the Ansar came forward, and they said: We, O Messenger of God? He said: So be in the mouth of the people. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions had gone down to the people from the valley, and when he came out The two men went to the mouth of the people. Al-Ansari said to Al-Muhajiri: Which night would you most like to suffice for, the beginning or the end? He said: Rather, suffice me The first, he said: So the Muhajiri lay down and slept, and the Ansari stood up to pray, he said: The woman’s husband came, and when he saw the man’s figure, he knew that The poor of the people. He said: He shot him with an arrow and put it in it. He said: So he took it off and put it in and remained standing, praying. Then he shot him with another arrow and put it in. In it, he said: So he took it off and put it in it and stood standing and praying, then he returned for the third time and put it in it, so he took it off and put it in it, then he bowed and prostrated, then His companion jumped up and said, “Sit down, for I have been steadfast.” He jumped up, and when the man saw them, he knew that he had made a vow to him, so he ran away. When the immigrant saw what With the Ansari from the blood, he said: Glory be to God, did you not give me a gift when he shot you the first time? He said: I was reciting a surah, but I did not like to interrupt it? Until I finished it, then when he continued shooting, I knelt down and gave you permission, and I swear to God, had I not missed a gap, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded me. By keeping it, I would cut myself off before I cut it off or spent it.” This is the hadith of Muhammad bin Isa"
"37","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala’, Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Zuhri, and Sa’id bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Makhzoumi told us, they said: Sufyan told us, Abdul-Jabbar said: Al-A’mash said, and the other two said: On the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: “We used to pray with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” And peace be upon him, so we do not perform ablution from a place of footing.” Al-Makhzoumi said: “We used to perform ablution with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but we did not perform ablution from a place of footing.” Al-Zuhri said: “We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we did not perform ablution from a place where we can stand.” Abu Bakr said: This news has a reason that Al-Amash did not hear it, on the authority of a brother. I did not understand it at the time. Abu Hashim Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, Abdullah bin Idris told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Shaqiq, he said: Abdullah said, We did not wrap our hair or clothes during prayer, nor did we perform ablution from a place of footing.” Ziyad bin Ayyub narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Al-Amash narrated to us, Shaqiq narrated to me, or I narrated on his authority, on the authority of Abdullah, something similar."
"38","Ahmad bin Abdah al-Dhabi told us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zaid, told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “ate a bone or ate meat, then prayed but did not perform ablution.” Abu Bakr said: The narration of Hammad bin Zayd is not connected with a connected chain of narration. We made a mistake in narrating it, for it is between Hisham bin Urwa and Muhammad bin Amr. Ibn Ataa, Wahb Ibn Kaysan. It was also narrated by Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan and Abdah bin Suleiman."
"39","Muhammad bin Bashar Bandar told us, Yahya told us, Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Ali bin Abdullah bin Abbas told me On the authority of Ibn Abbas. H and Hisham, on the authority of Wahb bin Kaysan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. H and Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ate bread And meat or sweat, then he prayed but did not perform ablution.”"
"40","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, he said: Wahb bin Kaysan told me, On the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. H Hisham said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Ali bin Abdullah bin Abbas, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. H Hisham said: Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdullah bin Abbas told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. “He ate some sweat, then he prayed but did not perform ablution.” This is the hadith of Al-Zuhri"
"41","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala al-Sadfi told us, Ibn Wahb told us, that Malik bin Anas told him. H Abu Musa told us, Ruh, meaning Ibn Ubadah, told us, Malik told us, on the authority of Zaid, who is Ibn Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yasar, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “ate a shoulder of a sheep, then prayed but did not perform ablution.”"
"42","Ahmad bin Abdah al-Dhabi told us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi, told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. “He saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performing ablution from a young bull, then he saw him eating the shoulder of a sheep, then he prayed but did not perform ablution.”"
"43","Musa bin Sahl al-Ramli told us, Ali bin Ayyash told us, Shuaib bin Abi Hamza told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Abdullah, he said: “The last of the two commands of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was to abandon ablution from anything that has touched fire.”"
"44","Bundar told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Zainab, the daughter of Umm Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “ate a shoulder, then prayed and did not touch water.”"
"45","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever swears an oath and says in his oath: By Al-Lat, let him say: There is no god but God, and whoever says to his companion: Come, I will gamble with you, and let him give something in charity.” Abu Bakr said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not command the one who swears by al-Lat, nor the one who says to his friend: “Come.” I beg you to perform ablution, as the news indicates that obscenity is in logic, and what a person is prohibited from saying does not require ablution, contrary to the saying Whoever claims that bad speech requires ablution?"
"46","Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Jawhari told us, I am Abu Asim, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Wahb bin Kaysan, On the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “drank milk, then rinsed his mouth.”"
"47","Muhammad bin Aziz Al-Ayli told us that Salama bin Rawh told them, on the authority of Aqeel, who is Ibn Khalid, and Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us Al-Sana’ani, Mu’tamar, meaning Ibn Sulayman, told us, saying: I heard Mu’mar. H Muhammad bin Bashar Bandar and Abu Musa told us, saying: Yahya, who is Ibn Sa’id, told us. Al-Awza’i, all of them, told us about Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, drank milk, rinsed his mouth, and said: “It has “Heavy.” Al-San’ani said in his hadith: Or it is fat, and Bundar said: It is fat."
"48","Muhammad bin Bashar narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, Ibn Ajlan narrated to us. H And Yahya bin Hakim told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, he said: I heard my father, speaking, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “My eyes sleep but my heart does not sleep.”"
"49","Yunus bin Abd al-Ala al-Sadfi told us, Ibn Wahb told us, that Malik told him, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman told him that he asked Aisha: How was the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not pray more than eleven rak’ahs in Ramadan or at any other time, so do not ask about Their beauty and length, then he prays four, so do not ask about their beauty and length, then he prays three. Aisha said: So I said: O Messenger of God, Do you sleep before you feel stressed? He said: “O Aisha, my eyes sleep but my heart does not sleep.”"
"50","Ali bin Hajar Al-Saadi narrated to us, Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar, narrated to us, Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, he said: “When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went further with the doctrine.”"
"51","Bundar told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Abu Jafar Al-Khutmi told us, Bundar said: I said to Yahya: What is his name? He said: Umayr bin Yazid. Amara bin Khuzaymah and Al-Harith bin Fudayl told me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Qarad, who said: “I went out with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I saw him come out of the toilet, and whenever he wanted something he would go away.”"
"52","Abu Hashim Ziyad bin Ayyub narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: You saw me walking With the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ended up standing in a crowd of people, so he got up and urinated like one of you urinates, so I went to get away from him, and he said: \"Come closer to him,\" so I approached him until I stood up after him until he had finished."
"53","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Mahdi bin Maimun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Yaqoub, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jaafar, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, loved to cover himself in his need as a target.” Or a palm tree.” Abu Bakr said: I heard Muhammad bin Aban saying: I heard Ibn Idris saying: I said to Shu’bah: What do you say about Mahdi bin Maymun? He said: Trustworthy. I said: He told me about Salam al-Alawi. He said: I saw Aban bin Abi Ayyash with Anas bin Malik writing in Spurga, he said: The upper ladder that was seen means the crescent before the people? Abu Bakr said: Muhammad bin Abi Ya’qub is Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Ya’qub. His lineage to his grandfather is the one he said about. Shu’bah: Muhammad bin Abi Ya’qub, the leader of Banu Tamim, told me."
"54","Nasr bin Ali Al-Jahdhami narrated to us, Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, meaning Al-Taffawi, narrated to us, Hisham bin Urwa narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: Sawda bint Zam’a was a powerful woman. Whenever she went out to relieve herself at night, she would supervise the women, and Omar saw her. Ibn Al-Khattab, and he said: See how you get out? By God, you will not hide from us when you come out. So I mentioned that to the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and there was a vein in his hand, but he did not respond. The sweat dripped from his hand until the revelation was complete, and he said: “Indeed, God has given you a license to go out to meet your needs.” Abu Bakr told us, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham, similarly"
"55","Yusuf bin Musa told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by One of the walls of Mecca or Medina, then he heard the sound of two people being tortured in their graves, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They are being tortured. And they will not be punished for any major matter.” Then he said: “Yes, one of them was not covering himself from his urine, and the other used to go about gossiping.” Then he called for a newspaper and broke it. Two shards, and a shard was placed on each grave, and it was said to him: Why did you do this? He said: “Perhaps He will make it easy for them as long as they do not dry out or until they dry out.”"
"56","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Waki’ narrated to us, Al-Amash narrated to us, I heard a mujahid narrating: On the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger passed by May God bless him and grant him peace, with two graves, the same."
"57","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us, Al-Zuhri told us. H Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makhzoumi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ Al-Laythi, on the authority of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not face the Qiblah while defecating or urinating, and do not turn away from it, but rather face the Qiblah when you are defecating or urinating, and do not turn away from it, but rather face toward the east or the west.” Abu Ayyub said: So we came to the Levant and found latrines that had been built towards the Qiblah, so we turned away from them and asked God for forgiveness. This is the wording of the hadith of Abdul Jabbar."
"58","Muhammad bin Bashar narrated to us, Wahb, meaning Ibn Jarir bin Hazim, narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Ishaq speaking, on the authority of Aban bin Saleh, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from receiving “The kiss was made by urinating, and I saw him facing it a year before he was caught.”"
"59","Muhammad bin Bashar and Yahya bin Hakim told us, saying: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah. H, Nasr bin Ali Al-Jahdhami told us, Abd al-Ala told us, Ubaid Allah told us. H Muhammad bin Muawiyah Al-Baghdadi told us, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed. H Muhammad bin Al-Walid told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab told us, meaning Al-Thaqafi, he said: I heard Yahya bin Saeed. H Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Makhzoumi told us, Abu Hisham, meaning Al-Makhzoumi, told us, Wahib told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, and Yahya Bin Saeed, and Ismail bin Umayyah. H Ahmed bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim Al-Barqi told us, Ibn Abi Maryam told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, he told me Ibn Ajlan, Bundar said in his hadith, he said, he told me, and Yahya bin Hakim said: he said, he told us, and Muhammad bin al-Walid said: he said, I heard, The others said: On the authority of Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban, on the authority of his uncle Wasi’ ibn Hibban, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “I entered upon Hafsa, Umar’s daughter. So I went up to the back of the house and supervised the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, while he was alone, facing the qiblah and heading towards the Levant.” This is the wording of the hadith of Abdul-Ala, and in the report of Abu Hisham: facing the qiblah."
"60","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Safwan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Dhakwan, on the authority of Marwan Al-Asghar, he said: I saw Ibn Umar snort He made his mount facing the Qiblah, then he sat to urinate on it. I said: “Abu Abd al-Rahman, isn’t this forbidden?” He said: “Yes, that is only forbidden in space, so if there is something between you and the qiblah that covers you, then there is no problem.”"
"61","Ahmad bin Abdah al-Dhabi told us, Abu Awanah told us. H. Salam bin Junada told us, Waki’ told us both, on the authority of Al-A’mash. H Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah. H. Bishr bin Khaled Al-Askari told us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ja’far, told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Sulayman, who is Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, On the authority of Hudhayfah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “came to a people’s tent and urinated while standing, then he performed ablution and wiped over his socks.”"
"62","Nasr bin Ali told us, Al-Fudayl bin Sulaiman told us, I am Abu Hazim, he said: I saw Sahl bin Saad urinating standing up, for he narrated That was upon him, and he said: “I have seen someone who is better than me do it.”"
"63","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak Al-Mukhurami narrated to us, Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Abi Suleiman, and Asim bin Bahdala, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “came to Sabat The son of so-and-so, he spread his legs and urinated standing up.”"
"64","Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makhzoumi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Uqba, and Ibn Abi Harmala, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Usama bin Zaid told me that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “urinated in the people on the night of Muzdalifah,” and he did not say: “Burning.” Water"
"65","Ahmad bin Abdah al-Dhabi told us, Sulaym, meaning Ibn Akhdar, told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I was supporting the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, against my chest. He called for a basin, urinated in it, then turned away and died.”"
"66","Saeed bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Makhzoumi told us, Sufyan, who is Ibn Uyaynah, told us, on the authority of Ayoub Al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, On the authority of Abu Hurairah. H, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. H, Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala’ narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zannad, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Uthman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “None of you should urinate in water that does not flow, then take a bath in it.” Al-Makhzoumi said: In standing water, then wash with it."
"67","Ali bin Hajar narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, Al-Ala bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Beware of the two curses or the two who curse.” It was said: What are they? He said: “The one who hides in the path of people or in their shadow.” Abu Bakr said: “I only inferred that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, meant when he said:” Or their shadow: the shade with which they take shade when they sit in their gatherings, according to the news of Abdullah bin Jaafar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He loves what he uses to cover himself for his needs: a tree or a stalk of a palm tree, since the goal is a wall, and a stalk of palm trees is a group of palm trees. The orchard was called Haish because of the large number of its trees, and the target is almost nowhere to be found without a shadow, except at the setting of the sun. As for the Haish, it is a palm tree. There is no time during the day when it does not have shade, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, considered it desirable for a person to cover himself in the excrement. By the target and the wanderer, even if they have a shadow."
"68","Ali bin Khashram told us, Issa, meaning Ibn Yunus, told us, on the authority of Muammar bin Rashid, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abu Qatada, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you urinates, he should not touch his penis with his right hand.”"
"69","Muhammad bin Bashar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi narrated to us, and Muhammad bin Jaafar narrated to us, they said: Shu’bah narrated to us. H Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani told us, Khalid, meaning Ibn al-Harith, told us. Shu’bah told us. H, Yahya bin Hakim told us, Ibn Abi Adi told us, Shu’bah told us. H Yahya bin Hakim also told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard an-Nadhar bin Anas He narrates, on the authority of Zayd ibn Arqam, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “These halls are dying, so if one of you enters them, let him say: Oh God, I seek refuge in You from evil and evil things.” This is the hadith of Bundar, except that he said: On the authority of al-Nadr ibn Anas, and so Yahya ibn Hakim said in the hadith of Ibn Abi Adi, on the authority of al-Nadr ibn Anas"
"70","Abu Abdullah Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, Ziyad bin Al-Hasan bin Furat told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to defecate, so he said: “Bring me three stones.” Then I found for him two stones and donkey dung. He took the two stones and threw away the dung, and said, “It is an abomination.”"
"71","Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, On the authority of Hilal bin Iyadh, he said: Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri told me, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The two men shall not go out They throw the excrement, revealing their private parts and talking, for God Almighty abhors that.” Muhammad bin Yahya narrated to us, Sallam bin Ibrahim, meaning Al-Warraq, narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah bin Ammar narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Many, on the authority of Iyad bin Hilal, with this chain of transmission and something similar. Abu Bakr said: This sheikh is Iyaad ibn Hilal. Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated from him without hadith, and I think it is an illusion from Ikrimah bin Ammar when he said: On the authority of Hilal bin Iyadh"
"72","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Abi Fudaik told us, Al-Dahhak bin Uthman told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man should not look at a man’s private parts, and you should not look at a man’s private parts.” “A woman is exposed to the private parts of a woman, and a man does not open to a man in the same garment, and a woman does not open to a woman in the same garment.”"
"73","Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, Abu Dawud Al-Hafari told us, on the authority of Sufyan. H Muhammad bin Bashar narrated to us, Abu Ahmad, meaning Al-Zubair, narrated to us, Sufyan Al-Thawri narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “A man passed by the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was urinating, and he greeted him, but he did not return his greeting.”"
"74","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi and Yusuf bin Musa told us, they said: Waki’ narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Salman, said: Some of the polytheists said to him, and they were mocking him: I see your friend teaching you even nonsense, he said Salman: “Yes, we are commanded not to face the Qiblah, not to cleanse ourselves with our oaths, and not to be satisfied with three stones, in which there is no debris or Bone. However, Al-Dawraqi said: Some polytheists said to Salman"
"75","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Yunus bin Yazid told me. H Yunus also told us, Ibn Wahb told us, that Malik told him. H Utbah bin Abdullah told us, Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, Yunus told us. H Yahya bin Hakim told us, Othman bin Omar told us, Yunus, and Malik told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever performs ablution, let him spit it out, and whoever performs ablution, let him spit it out.” In the hadith of Ibn Al-Mubarak: Abu Idris Al-Khawlani told me that he heard Abu Hurairah. I heard Yunus, saying: Ibn Uyaynah was asked about the meaning of his saying: And whoever performs prayers should pray witr. He said: Then Ibn Uyaynah remained silent, so he was told: Should I be satisfied with what Malik said? He said: What did Malik say? It was said: Malik said: Istijmaar, covering with stones, and Ibn Uyaynah said: It is just like me and like Malik, as the first said: And Ibn al-Laboun If he is stuck in a horn he is not able to straighten the hole, the pins"
"76","It was narrated by Yusuf bin Musa, it was narrated by Jarir, on the authority of Al-Amash. H. Ya’qub bin Ibrahim, Isa bin Yunus, Al-A’mash told us. H Abu Musa told us, from Abdul Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “If one of you performs the ritual ijmaarah, let him perform it three times.”"
"77","Abu Ghassan Malik bin Saad Al-Qaysi narrated to us, narrated to us Ruh, meaning Ibn Ubadah, Abu Amir Al-Khazzaz narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When one of you performs the prayer, let him perform the Witr, for God is a Witr and loves Witr. Do you not see the heavens as seven, and the Earth “Seven days, and tawaaf is seven days,” and he mentioned some things."
"78","On the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani, on the authority of Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, on the authority of Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah al-Dastawa’i, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir. On the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father Abi Qatada, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you drinks, do not He should breathe into the vessel, and when he comes to the toilet, he should not touch his penis with his right hand, and if he wipes himself, he should not wipe it with his right hand.”"
"79","Ali bin Hajar told us, Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i. H Nasr bin Marzuq Al-Masry told us, Amr, meaning Ibn Abi Salamah, told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi, told me. Many, Abdullah bin Abi Qatada Al-Ansari narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “If “One of you should not touch his penis with his right hand, or clean himself with his right hand, or breathe into a vessel.” This is the hadith of Amr bin Abi Salamah, and Ali bin Hajar said about all of them: On the authority of"
"80","On the authority of Muhammad bin Bashar, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I am to you like a father to his child. None of you should face the Qiblah or turn away from it, meaning in He does not defecate, and he should not clean himself without three stones that do not contain dung or sap.”"
"81","Abdullah bin Saeed bin Al-Ashjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Numayr, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Salman He said: The polytheists said: Your companion has taught you to the point that he is about to teach you nonsense. He said: Yes, he forbade us from facing the Qiblah, or We cleanse ourselves with our oath, or with the bone, or with the return, and he said: “None of you is sufficient without three stones.”"
"82","Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Abd al-A’la bin Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Dawud. ح وَحَدَّثَنَا أَبُو هَاشِمٍ زِيَادُ بْنُ أَيُّوبَ ، نا يَحْيَى يَعْنِي ابْنَ أَبِي زَائِدَةَ ، قَالَ: أَخْبَرَنِي دَاوُدُ بْنُ أَبِي هِنْدَ ، عَنْ عَامِرٍ ، He said: I asked Alqamah: Did Ibn Masoud witness with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the night of the jinn? Alqamah said: I asked Ibn Masoud, and I said: Did any of you witness with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the night of the jinn? فَقَالَ: لا، وَلَكِنْ كُنَّا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ذَاتَ لَيْلَةٍ، فَفَقَدْنَاهُ، فَالْتَمَسْنَاهُ فِي الأَوْدِيَةِ وَالشِّعَابِ، فَقُلْنَا: اسْتُطِيرَ أَوِ اغْتِيلَ، قَالَ: فَبِتْنَا بِشَرِّ لَيْلَةٍ بَاتَ بِهَا قَوْمٌ، فَلَمَّا أَصْبَحْنَا، فَإِذَا هُوَ جَاءٍ مِنْ قِبَلِ حِرَاءَ، قَالَ: فَقُلْنَا: يَا Messenger of God, we lost you, so we looked for you but did not find you, so we spent a night in which people spent the night. He said: “The caller of the jinn came to me, so I went with him and recited عَلَيْهِمُ الْقُرْآنَ\"، قَالَ: فَانْطَلَقَ بِنَا فَأَرَانَا نِيرَانَهُمْ، قَالَ: وَسَأَلُوهُ الزَّادَ، فَقَالَ:\" لَكُمْ كُلُّ عَظْمٍ ذُكِرَ اسْمُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ يَقَعُ فِي أَيْدِيكُمْ أَوْفَرُ مَا يَكُونُ لَحْمًا، وَكُلُّ بَعْرٍ عَلَفًا لِدَوَابِّكُمْ\"، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ:\" فَلا تَسْتَنْجُوا بِهِمَا فَإِنَّهَا طَعَامُ “Your brothers.” This is the hadith of Abdul-Ala, and in the hadith of Ibn Abi Zaida, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not cleanse yourself with a bone or بِالْبَعْرِ، فَإِنَّهُ زَادُ إِخْوَانِكُمْ مِنَ الْجِنِّ\""
"83","Narrated to us Muhammad bin Yahya, narrated to us Ismail bin Abi Uwais, narrated to me by my father, on the authority of Sharhabeel bin Saad, on the authority of Uwaim bin Sa’idah Al-Ansari, then Al-Ajlani said that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the people of Quba: “Indeed, God has praised you for your purity, and said: There are men who love to They purify themselves in Surat Al-Tawbah, verse 108 until the verse is completed.” Then he said to them: “What is this purification?” They said: We do not know anything except that we had neighbors from The Jews, and they used to wash their backs from excrement, so We washed them just as they washed them."
"84","It was narrated to me by Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi, it was narrated to me by Ibn Ulayya, it was narrated to me by Ruh bin Al-Qasim, it was narrated to me by Ataa bin Abi Maimunah, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, He said: “Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, defecated due to a need, I would bring him water and he would wash himself with it.”"
"85","Narrated by Muhammad bin Khalid bin Khaddash Al-Zahrani, narrated by Salem bin Qutayba, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Maimunah, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “when he went to do what he needed, I would go with him with a crutch and a tool, and when he went out, he would wipe with water. And he performed ablution from the ablution.”"
"86","Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad al-Anbari told us, my father told me, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abu Muadh, he said: I heard Anas, saying: “It was When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out for his needs, I and another boy followed him with a cup of water.” Abu Bakr said: This Abu Muadh is: Ata bin Abi Maimunah."
"87","On the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Walid, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ja’far, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Abi Maimunah, that he heard Anas ibn Malik say: “It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, enters the toilet, and a boy and I carry a tool of water and other things, and he cleans himself with water.”"
"88","Yusuf bin Musa told us, Waki’ told us. H. Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Abdullah bin Numayr told us. H And Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Khuza’i told us, Muhammad bin Bishr told us, they said: Zakariya told us, and he is the son of Abi Zaida, we Musab bin Shaybah, on the authority of Talq bin Habib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, that Aisha told him that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Ten of the things that are fitrah: trimming the mustache, inhaling water, using the siwak, growing the beard, plucking the armpits, shaving the pubic area, and trimming Water, cutting nails, and washing knuckles.” Abdah said in his hadith: And the tenth hour, I do not know what it is, except to rinse the mouth. In the hadith of Waki`, Mus`ab said: I forgot the tenth hour, unless it was rinsing the mouth. Waki` said: The water decreases, if he sprinkles it with water, it decreases. Ibn Rafi’ did not mention the tenth, nor did Sufyan, nor did he doubt."
"89","Muhammad bin Yahya narrated to us, Abu Nu’aym narrated to us, Aban bin Abdullah Al-Bajli narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Jarir narrated to me, on the authority of his father The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “entered the forest and relieved himself, then Jarir brought him a cup of water and he cleaned himself with it. He said: And he wiped \"His hand is in the dust\""
"90","Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Bukayr, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Yusuf bin Abi Burdah, on the authority of his father, he said: I went to see Aisha and heard her say: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out of the toilet, he would say: “Your forgiveness.” Muhammad ibn Aslam narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, similar to this."
"91","Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quti’ narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, narrated to us Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to perform ablution, and one of his wives said: O Messenger of God, I I performed ablution from this, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution and said: “Water cannot be made impure by anything.” This is the hadith of Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam"
"92","Ours is Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak Al-Mukhurami, Musa bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Masruqi, and Abu Al-Azhar Hawthara bin Muhammad Al-Basri, they said: Abu Usama told us, Al-Walid bin Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ja’far bin Al-Zubayr, that Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Omar told them that his father, Abdullah bin Omar, told them that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about water and what comes with it. Animals and wild animals. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the water is two small amounts, it does not carry impurity.” This is a Hawthara hadith. Musa bin Abdul Rahman said: On the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father, and he also said: “Nothing made him impure.” As for Al-Mukhrami, he told us about it briefly, and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the water is two drops, it will not hold water.” Wickedness,” and he did not mention the question of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about water and the wild animals and animals that accompany it."
"93","On the authority of Yunus bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Abdullah bin Wahb, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah, who told him that Abu Al-Sa'ib, the client of Hisham bin Zahra, narrated to him that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He does not wash “One of you is in stagnant water while he is junub.” He said: “How should he do it, Abu Hurairah?” He said: He takes it one by one"
"94","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Anas bin Iyaad told us, on the authority of Al-Harith, who is Ibn Abi Dhubab, on the authority of Ata’ bin Mina, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of you should urinate in standing water, then perform ablution or drink from it.”"
"95","Narrated by Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi, narrated by Ibn Aliya, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan. H Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Ibrahim bin Sadaqa told us. H. Ismail bin Bashir bin Mansour Al-Sulaymi, narrated to us, was narrated to us by Abd al-A’la. H Muhammad bin Yahya al-Quti’ told us, Muhammad bin Marwan told us, they said: Hisham bin Hassan told us. H Jamil bin Al-Hassan told us, he said: Muhammad bin Marwan told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The purification of one of you’s vessel if a dog licks in it is to wash it seven times, the first time with dirt.” Al-Dawraqi said: He started it with dirt, and Al-Quti’i said: He started it with dirt."
"96","On the authority of Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Purity If a dog licks your vessel, he must wash it seven times.”"
"97","Jamil bin Al-Hasan narrated to us, Abu Hammam narrated to us, meaning Muhammad bin Marwan, Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Abu Al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace: “If a dog drinks from a vessel, its purification must be washed seven times, the first with dirt.”"
"98","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Ismail bin Khalil told us, Ibn Ali told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Razin, and Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Kitten, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a dog licks the bowl of one of you, let him throw it away and wash it seven times.” “And if one of you’s hair is cut off, he should not walk on it until he repairs it.”"
"99","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala and Saeed bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Makhzoumi told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you wakes up from his sleep, he should not dip his hand in the vessel until he has washed it.” Thirdly, he does not know where his hand has spent the night.” This is the hadith of Abdul-Jabbar, except that he said: On the authority of Abu Hurairah, a narration"
"100","Muhammad bin Al-Walid brought us strange news, Muhammad bin Jaafar brought us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you wakes up from his sleep, he should not dip his hand in his vessel or in his ablution until he washes it, for he does not know where his hand came from.”"
"101","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Utbah bin Abi Utbah, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, that it was said to Omar bin Al-Khattab: Tell us about the hour of difficulty, Omar said: We left for Tabuk in extreme heat, and we stayed at a house in which we became so thirsty that we thought our necks would be cut off, even though it was A man goes to seek water and does not return until he thinks that his neck will be cut off. A man even slaughters his camel and squeezes its dung. So he drinks it and puts what remains on his liver. Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq said: O Messenger of God, God has taught you good in supplication, so pray for us. He said: “Do you like that?” He said: Yes, so he raised his hand and did not bring them back until the sky said, and it became dark, then it poured out, so they filled what they had, then We went to look but did not find her as she had passed the army. Abu Bakr said: If the water of excrement when squeezed out is impure, it is not permissible for a person to put it on his liver so that part of his body becomes impure. There is no pure water to wash the unclean area of it, so as for drinking impure water when there is fear of spoilage, if one does not drink that water, It is permissible to revive a soul by drinking impure water, since God Almighty has permitted, in the event of necessity, to revive a soul by eating dead animals and blood. And the meat of a pig if there is a fear of spoilage if one does not eat it, and carrion, blood, and the meat of a pig are impure and forbidden to the one who does not need it. It is permissible. For the one who is forced to revive himself by eating it, it is also permissible for the one who is forced to drink impure water to revive himself by drinking impure water if He feared harm to himself by giving up drinking it. As for putting impure water on some part of his body, there is knowledge that if he did not make that water The one who was impure on his body did not conceal the damage to himself, nor was it possible for him to touch his body with that impure water to revive himself thereby, nor did he have Pure water. He washes what is impure on his body with that water. This is not permissible, and there is no room for anyone to do it."
"102","Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris narrated to us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Jafar Al-Razi narrated to us, Sulayman bin Musafa bin Shaybah Al-Hajabi narrated to us, He said: I heard Mansour ibn Safiya bint Shaybah, narrating, on the authority of his mother Safiya, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said To them: “She is not unclean, she is like some of the household.” Meaning: the kitten"
"103","Na Muhammad bin Yahya, Na Ibrahim bin Al-Hakam Ibn Aban, my father told me, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Abu Qatada used to perform ablution from The vessel and the cat drinks from it.” And Ikrimah said and said, Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The cat is one of the household goods.”"
"104","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala al-Sadafi told us, Ibn Wahb told us that Malik told him, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah, who is the son of Abi Talha On the authority of Hamida bint Ubaid bin Rifa’ah, on the authority of Kabsha bint Ka’b bin Malik, who was under Ibn Abi Qatada, that Abu Qatada He went in to her, and she poured water for him to perform ablution, and a cat came to drink from it, so Abu Qatada poured the vessel for her until she drank. Kabsha said: He saw me looking at him and said: Do you wonder, my niece? She said: So I said: Yes, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not impure, but rather it is from those who come around you or \"rafts\""
"105","Narrated to us Abu Al-Khattab Ziyad bin Yahya Al-Hasani, narrated to us Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal, narrated to us Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a fly lands in the vessel of one of you, then there is a disease on one of its wings, and on the other A cure, and he protects himself with his wing that has the disease, so let him immerse it entirely, then snatch it away.”"
"106","We are Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala, we are Sufyan, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, saying: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, saying: “I fell ill Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to meet me and Abu Bakr while walking, and he found that I had fainted, so he performed ablution and poured it on me, so I woke up.” . I said: O Messenger of God, what should I do with my money? How do I spend my money? He did not answer me anything until “the verse of inheritance was revealed: If a man dies having no child, and he has a sister, then to her is half of what he left behind, Surah An-Nisa, verse 176.” He once said: Until the verse of Kalaala was revealed."
"107","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad narrated to us, Ubaida bin Humaid narrated to us, Al-Aswad bin Qais narrated to us, on the authority of Nabih Al-Anazi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: We traveled With the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then prayer came, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Is there no purity among the people?” He said: Then a man came. With water for treatment, he said: So he poured it into a cup and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution. He said: Then the people did the rest of the purification. He said: Wipe with it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard them and said: “On your messengers.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, struck his hand. In the cup in the bowl of water, then he said: “Perfectly purify yourself.” Jabir bin Abdullah said: And that which has cleared my sight. He said: And he had gone. His sight: I saw water springing from between the fingers of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he did not raise his hand until everyone had performed ablution. Ubaidah said: Al-Aswad said: I thought so. He said: We were two hundred or more."
"108","Narrated by Muhammad bin Rafi’, narrated by Abd al-Razzaq, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj. H Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Jawhari told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr bin Dinar told me, he said: My greatest knowledge, and what comes to my mind, is that Abu Al-Sha’a’a told me that he heard Ibn Abbas say that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He performs ablution thanks to Maimuna.”"
"109","Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Ahmad ibn Mani` told us, they said: Abu Ahmad, who is al-Zubairi, narrated to us. Sufyan narrated to us. H Utbah bin Abdullah told us, Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, Sufyan told us. H Salam bin Junada narrated to us, Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that A woman from the Prophet’s wives, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took a bath from ritual impurity, “so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed ablution or bathed from her bounty.” This is a comprehensive hadith, and Ahmad bin Mani’ said: “Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution from her bounty.” Abu Musa and Utbah bin Abdullah said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to perform ablution from her bounty, and she said to him, and he said: “Water does not \"Something defiles it\""
"110","On the authority of Yusuf bin Musa, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mis’ar ibn Kadam, on the authority of Al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, brings a vessel and I begin to drink while I am menstruating. Then he takes the vessel and places his mouth on a place in me, and I take So I bite it, then he puts his mouth on a place in me.” It was narrated by Salam bin Junada, it was narrated by Waki’, on the authority of Mas’ar, and Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, with this chain of transmission similar to it."
"111","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala al-Sadafi told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us that Malik told him, he said: Safwan bin Sulaym told me, on the authority of Sa`id bin Salamah, from the family of Ibn al-Azraq, said that Al-Mughirah bin Abi Burdah, who was from Banu Abd al-Dar, told him that he heard Abu Hurairah, He says: A man asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, we are sailing by sea and carrying a little water. We performed ablution with it when we were thirsty. Shall we perform ablution with sea water? He said: “Its water is pure, and its dead meat is lawful.” This is the hadith of Yunus, and Yahya bin Hakim said: On the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, and he did not say: From the family of Ibn al-Azraq, nor from Banu Abd al-Dar, and he said: We ride the sea for a while"
"112","Muhammad bin Yahya narrated to us, Ahmad bin Hanbal narrated to us, Abu al-Qasim bin Abi al-Zinad narrated to me, Ishaq bin Hazim narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Miqsim, he said Ahmad: meaning Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about the sea, and he said: “Its water is pure, and its dead is lawful.”"
"113","We have Muhammad bin Bashar, we have Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan, Ibn Abi Adi, Sahl, and Abdul Wahhab bin Abdul Majeed Al-Thaqafi. They said: Awf told us, on the authority of Abu Raja, Imran bin Husayn told us, he said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and he called so-and-so and he called Ali bin Abi Talib, and he said: “Go and seek water for us.” So they set off and met a woman between two rooftops or between two camel stalls, so they said She asked her: Where is the water? She said: My appointment with the water was yesterday at this hour. We left in a row, and he said to her: Go. She said: Where? They told her: To a messenger May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. She said: This is the one who is called al-Sabi’. They said to her: He is the one you mean. So they set off and brought her to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. They told him the hadith, and he said: Take her down from her camel. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for a vessel and put it in it. The mouths of the two mouthpieces or the two surfaces, they said: Then he rinsed his mouth, then he put it back in the mouths of the two mouthpieces or the two surfaces, then he released their mouths. Then it was called to the people, “Irrigate and draw water.” He mentioned the hadith in its length"
"114","Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Khuza’i told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to perform ablution from a waterskin, and he was told: It is a dead animal. He said: “His tanning removes any of its impurity, impurity, or uncleanness.”"
"115","It is narrated by Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani, it is narrated by Yazid, meaning Ibn Zuray’, it is said by Sa’id, it is narrated by Qatada, that Anas ibn Malik narrated to them, that people or Men from Ukal and Urainah came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the city. They spoke Islam and said: O Messenger of God, we are the people of We were not people of the countryside, so they invaded the city.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered them to bring animals and shepherds, and ordered them to They will go out there and drink of its urine and milk.” He mentioned the hadith in its length"
"116","We are Muhammad bin Bashar, we are Abdul Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, we are Shu`bah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Jabr bin Atik, He said: I heard Anas bin Malik say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to perform ablution with a shuttlecock, and bathe with five Makkikahs.” Abu Bakr said: The shuttle in this report is the mudd itself."
"117","Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdhani narrated to us from his book, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, and Yazid bin Abi Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The mudd is sufficient for ablution, and for ritual impurity. “The saa’.” A man said to him: This is not enough for us, Jabir. He said: It is enough for someone who is better than you and has more hair. Abu Bakr said in his saying, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “The mudd is sufficient for ablution”: an indication that the timing of the mudd of water for ablution That is sufficient, not that it is not permissible to decrease or add to it."
"118","It is narrated by Muhammad bin Al-Alaa bin Kurayb Al-Hamdani, it is narrated by Yahya bin Abi Zaidah, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ibn Zaid, and he is Habib bin Zaid, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “was brought two-thirds of a mudd, and he began to massage his arm.”"
"119","On the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Walid, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Jaafar, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God Almighty be pleased with him. On her authority, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I used to perform ablution from one vessel.”"
"120","Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani told us, from Abu Khalid, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “We used to perform ablution while men And women, and we wash our hands in one vessel at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"121","Narrated by Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani, narrated by al-Mu’tamir, who said: I heard Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah, that, “He looked at the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him and his companions purifying themselves, and the women with them, the men and women, from one vessel, all of them purifying themselves from it.”"
"122","From Muhammad bin Bashar, from Abu Dawud, from Kharijah Ibn Musab, from Yunus, from Al-Hasan, from Utai ibn Damrah Al-Saadi, from Ubayy Ibn Ka’b, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, there is a devil who performs ablution, who is called a deceiver, so beware of the whisperer of water.”"
"123","Muhammad bin Yahya and Muhammad bin Rafi’ narrated to us. Muhammad bin Yahya said: I heard Abd al-Razzaq. Ibn Rafi’ said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated us. Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God Almighty be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in His illness in which he died: “They poured on me seven sacrifices, the sacks of which were not loosened, that I might rest and be alone with the people.” Aisha said: So we made him sit in Hafsa’s copper furnace, and we poured water on him from them, until he started indicating to us, “You have done this.” Then he went out. Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated it to us once, Abd al-Razzaq narrated it to us once, Muammar narrated to us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, something similar, other than He did not say “from copper,” nor did he say “then he left.”"
"124","Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dhabi told us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, informed us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called With ablution, a cup was brought with water in it. I think he said: a glass cup. So he put his fingers in it, and the people began to perform ablution first and last. So I numbered them between seventy and eighty, and I looked at the water as if it were springing from between his fingers.” Abu Bakr said: This news was narrated by more than one person, on the authority of Hammad bin Zaid, and they said: There is no doubt about the place of the glass. Muhammad bin Yahya narrated to us, Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, with this hadith, and he said in the hadith of Suleiman bin Harith: A glass cup was brought, and he said in Hadith of Abu Al-Numan: With a glass vessel. Abu Bakr said: By Al-Rahrah: it is only the wide one of the glass vessels, not the deep one."
"125","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawrqi told us, Hushaym told us, Husayn told us, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: The people were thirsty on the Day of Hudaybiyyah, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had before him a bowl from which to perform ablution, when the people gathered toward him. He said: He said: “What is the matter with you?” They said: We have no water to perform ablution, and we only drink what is before you. He said: So he put his hands in the place of prayer and prayed for what God willed. He called, he said: Then he made the water gush out from between his fingers like springs, he said: So we drank and performed ablution, he said: I said to Jabir: How old were you? He said: We were fifteen hundred, and if we had been one hundred thousand, it would have been enough for us."
"126","On the authority of Muhammad ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Wahb ibn Jarir, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Amir, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought May God bless him and grant him peace, with a small bowl, so he performed ablution from it.” So I said to Anas: Did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, perform ablution at every prayer? He said: Yes, I said: And you? He said: We used to perform the prayers with ablution."
"127","On the authority of Yahya bin Hakim, on the authority of Ibn Adi, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: A house in a house. My aunt is Maimuna, so I stayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, how he prayed at night.” He urinated, then washed his face and hands, then slept, then got up He released the baghook, poured it into the bowl or the bowl, and performed ablution between the two ablutions, and stood up to pray, so I stood up and performed ablution. So I came to his left, and he took me and placed me on his right.”"
"128","Abu Yunus al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid, meaning Ibn Abdullah, narrated to us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “We commanded The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered covering the ablution, holding waterskins, and filling the vessel.” Abu Bakr said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, applied the name ablution to the water with which one performs ablution, and this is of the type that I learned about. In more than one place in our books is it that the Arabs assign the noun to the thing at the beginning in the same manner as the word follows it, since water before He performs ablution with it. The name “ablution” was given to it, because it refers to one who performs ablution with it."
"129","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr. H And Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, that he heard Jabir, saying: Tell me Abu Humaid, he said: I brought the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a cup of unfermented milk from the infusion, and he said: “Have you not fermented it, even if you show it with a stick?” Abu Humayd said: He only ordered the doors to be closed at night, and he only ordered the water vessels to be fermented at night, and Al-Darimi said: He only ordered the vessels to be fermented at night. It was brewed at night, and the vessels were to be rested at night, and he did not mention the doors."
"130","Ahmad bin Mansour al-Ramadi told us, Ibn Hajjaj, meaning Ibn Muhammad, told us: Ibn Jurayj said: Abu al-Zubayr told me that He heard Jabir bin Abdullah say: Abu Humaid said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, only commanded the waterways to be leaned against at night, and the doors to be kept.” \"closed at night\""
